                <pb facs="0874" n="788" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg788"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hill to Mr.
                            Bowen.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-11-29"><hi rendition="#italic">November 29,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hill instructs Mr. Bowen, in the event of possible withdrawal of British
                    legation, but not until after being requested by the British minister, to ask
                    the Venezuelan Government to acquiesce in Mr. Bowen’s taking temporary charge of
                    British interests and exercising the good offices usual in such cases.)</p>
            </div>
